# ThoughtStream - Digital Diary Application 
- Name: Silas McCloud
- Email: silas.mccloud@wsu.edu
- Date: 4/25/2026
- Git Repo: https://github.com/Microgoober/CS483-TopicsInCS

## Prerequisites
- Node.js (v16 or higher)
- MongoDB (local or Atlas)
- Google Cloud Console account (for OAuth credentials)
- OpenWeather API key (optional, for weather feature)

## Environment Setup
### Backend (.env)
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret
OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=your_openweather_api_key

### Frontend (.env) 
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id
VITE_OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=your_openweather_api_key

## Installation & Running
### Backend
```bash
cd thoughtstream-backend
npm install
npm run dev
# Runs #
```

### Frountend
```bash
cd thoughtstream-frontend
npm install
npm run dev
# Runs #
```

## Features
    Google OAuth 2.0 authentication
    JWT-based session management
    Create, Read, Update, Delete diary entries
    Weather widget with location-based weather
    Tags and reflections for entries
    Responsive design

## API Endpoints
POST     /api/auth/google    Google OAuth login
GET      /api/diary          Get all user entries
POST     /api/diary          Create new entry
PUT      /api/diary/:id      Update entry
DELETE   /api/diary/:id      Delete entry

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: React 18, Vite, React Router, Axios, Google OAuth
- **Backend**: Node.js, Express, MongoDB, JWT, Google Auth Library